            <div xml:id="d276">

                <pb facs="0586" n="554" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v19/pg554"/>

                <head>276. Memorandum From Director of Central Intelligence Dulles to the President’s Special
                    Assistant for National Security Affairs (Gray)<anchor n="0" xml:id="d276-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1959-03-31">March 31,
                    1959</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>[<hi rendition="#italic">less than 1 line of source text not
                            declassified</hi>] Resistance Program</item>
                </list>
                <p>1. Referring to your recent conversation on 30 March concerning my proposal by
                    memorandum of 27 March 1959 on the above subject,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d276-f2"
                    /> I <pb facs="0587" n="555" xml:id="pg555"/> wish to assure you that full
                    consideration has been given to the points that you have raised.</p>
                <p>[<hi rendition="#italic">3 paragraphs (21 lines of source text) not
                        declassified</hi>]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Allen W.
                                Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
